### Case: token-issue — identity has to exist before it can be attributed.
### Expect 200 with access_token / token_type / expires_in. See solution 01.
###
### Note for analytics: token requests are captured too. An app requesting a fresh
### token more than once per 12 minutes (with a 900s TTL) is not caching, and is
### quietly making this your busiest route. That query is chart 10 in ../charts.md.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token
authorization: Basic {{BASE64(CLIENT_ID:CLIENT_SECRET)}}
content-type: application/json

### curl equivalent:
###   curl -i -X POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token \
###     -u '{{CLIENT_ID}}:{{CLIENT_SECRET}}' \
###     -H 'content-type: application/json'
